Patch 0087: DonHotState, the fields of the inline guest dispatch path in one standard-layout struct owned by PS2Runtime.
What: new runtime/don_hot_state.h. EeScheduler's eeCycle, nextFastPathCycle, iopPendingEeCycles, iopBatchEeCycles,
dispatchCount, fastPathCount, pendingEeTimerInterrupts, checkpointPending and unwinding; PS2Memory's three EE-timer driver
fields (pending cycles, cycles to event, irq mask); PS2Runtime's stopRequested; and the dense function table (base, end,
slots, pointer) and the dispatch-history flag move into it. EeScheduler and PS2Memory hold a pointer (PS2Memory has its own
copy until PS2Runtime binds it). dispatchGuestBranch now reads only DonHotState (plus the scheduler call checkpointDue).
Statements, their order and every value are unchanged; no behaviour change. static_asserts pin the layout (size 104) that the
game module header (work/t605/abi/don_guest_abi.h) mirrors.
Verified: see work/t605/NOTES.md (fight_practice route, state hash equal to work/baseline/, perf_fight vs baseline).
Origin: original to this project.
